  "2026-10-24T13:10:39.618Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/154 . Product commit 8c1e899 contains the exact-bound SDK resolution fix, runtime version assertions, newer-only API regression, docs, emitted output and recreated tracker evidence. Post-commit repository identity/privacy scan passed 4/4. The complete staged diff had zero absolute filesystem paths, private network addresses, local username or hostname matches. Both local release gates already passed 367/367 with unchanged thresholds. CI must finish the full npm and Bun gates on Node 22 and 26 at the final head; no merge or release is authorized. Claim released for orchestrator review; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-24T14:29:04.798Z",codex-agent,"Review round: reproduce the empty-module fallback accepting unresolved SDK namespace imports, remove fabricated declarations, bind all SDK resolution to each selected published exports map, and add a two-bound mutation table plus an intentionally blinded-resolution self-test. Verify targeted tests, typecheck, lint, behavioral revert, and exact pushed CI npm/Bun release gates. Remote branch is current and already contains origin/main; no merge is needed."
  "2026-10-24T14:36:15.440Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now removes the empty declaration and delegates exports resolution to real TypeScript namespace probes scoped to the selected SDK, with no paths mapping in the probes. Only natively resolved files are rebound into external declarations. Probe failures retain real TypeScript codes even when dependency skipLibCheck would hide an unresolved import. Mutation controls cover eight cases at both 2026.10.17 and 2026.10.24: nonexistent subpath, removed exported subpath, misspelled package (TS2307); missing named/type-only exports (TS2305); type exported without a runtime value (TS2693); type-only import used as a value (TS1361); default versus namespace import (TS1192). Good authoring/read/namespace consumers must pass. Additional tests cover minimum-only subpath removal, hidden unresolved external imports, native string/conditional/wildcard/null/missing-file exports, and self-test rejection of both a blind compiler and a stubbed resolution probe. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks passed before final behavioral verification."
  "2026-10-24T14:39:06.773Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only sdk-contracts.ts with its pre-review HEAD implementation; kept all new tests and docs unchanged. Ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"resolution self-test|external declaration subpaths|native SDK exports\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts. Exit 1, all 3 regressions failed: mutation table detected only 12/16 drifts (nonexistent and removed namespace subpaths were accepted); external minimum-only removal reported 0 drift rows instead of 1; native null export crashed in the old exports parser. Immediately restored the fixed source in a finally block and verified its bytes matched the saved fix. Tests import the TypeScript source, so no reverted build artifact was needed. Earlier fixed checker suite passed 10/10 with 100% module lines/branches/functions; the final added exports and resolution-stub controls passed 2/2. Running the complete registered suite after restoration."
